    {
      "id": 18,
      "type": "text",
      "title": "Reading this dashboard",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 12,
        "x": 12,
        "y": 33
      },
      "options": {
        "mode": "markdown",
        "content": "**Metric types on this page**\n\n- `gym_http_requests_total` \u2014 **Counter**, only ever increases. Always wrapped in `rate()`; the raw value is meaningless because it resets on restart.\n- `gym_http_requests_in_flight` \u2014 **Gauge**, current value, read directly.\n- `gym_http_request_duration_seconds` \u2014 **Histogram**, cumulative buckets. `histogram_quantile()` interpolates a percentile from them.\n\n**The time window.** Every percentile here is over `[5m]`: a sliding 5-minute window ending at each point. A shorter window reacts faster and is noisier; a longer one is smoother and hides brief spikes. `rate()` needs at least 4 scrapes in its window \u2014 at a 15s scrape interval, nothing below `[1m]` is trustworthy."
      }
    }
